PaymentOrdersAndTheOneSlotTest
├── when a named payee refuses the native asset
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should hold the one attempt slot against another set
├── when the holder cancels the blocked attempt
│   └── it should free the slot for a new attempt that runs
├── when the refusing payee later accepts
│   └── it should run the same handover and pay the payee
├── when an open token order pays whoever executes
│   └── it should pay the token amount to the caller
├── when an open native order pays whoever executes
│   └── it should pay the native amount to the caller
├── when an open order has no amount
│   └── it should run three calls and pay nobody
└── when the account is short of the native asset
    ├── it should revert
    └── it should run the same handover once the account is funded
